<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambracian Gulf</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gulf of Arta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ambracian Gulf, now the Gulf of Arta, is an inlet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. In antiquity it was bordered by Ambracia to the north and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acarnania">Acarnania</a> to the south, and its narrow mouth at Actium saw Octavian's victory over Antony and Cleopatra in 31 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambracian-gulf.jpg" alt="Ambracian Gulf" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EFS_highres_STS066_STS066-101-39.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
